Z||000010||4UMLA1||11-26-2001||08:46 PM||||I got mine from a car dealer in Yorktown VA, paid $3,500.00 for the car and it was a steal, trust me <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  I had been looking for one for a while and I really wanted  a GT bad.  My girlfriend was driving around with her sister one day and saw this car in a lot.  She called me and I drove down to the lot with stars in my eyes.  Talked to the guy, test drove the car (this was my first time driving a GT Fiero) as soon as I started it up, it was mine!  The car is perfect, a lady had owned it all her life, so that will tell you how it has been driven and taken care of, anyway here is a picture of it.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://members.aol.com/luv4rez/images/10%20fiero%20gt%20.jpg"> ||||reg||6
Z||000011||Pyric||11-26-2001||11:40 PM||||Well, I got mine for nothing!  You heard me. The guy told me if I could fix it's problem with miss-firing, it was mine.    <P>I bought a $35 Throttle position sensor and 'Bang' my own 85 GT. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>So in actuality, mine cost $35.  Ticked him off something awful.  He had just spent $1500 to drop a new engine in it.  Only had 12 miles on it when I got it.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  ||||reg||1
