Z||000019||LoW_KeY||11-27-2001||07:03 PM||||16.4 haha.. sorry I just love car mag stats, I was getting 15.5 at 90 mph with my old 2.8 and a crappy clutch, couldn't launch the car off the line.. it wanted to studder.<P>If I didn't have that problem I could have probably managed 14.5-14.8 yeah call me crazy, but that 2.8 was strong, very strong, but I don't regret doing the new swap because I've done a few mods here and there and it keeps getting faster  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><P>all and all maybe I was lucky who knows? but my friends 2.8 hauls some major butt! <P>I can say this car is fun and waaaayyy under estimated, if something is wrong with performance its a good potential for 3.4, 3.8 or V8  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Like I said before maybe I got lucky on the fiero I owned cause I've rode in a few other V6's and they didn't have the spunk like my old 2.8 had.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/kc.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000020||Oreif||11-27-2001||08:42 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by BlackStang95:<BR><B>1988   Pontiac Fiero GT                       8.7            16.4<P>If that's only .1 seconds slower all fieros are pretty damned slow.  I read many places the 88's weighed a bit over 3000 pounds (even with my stang fyi).  </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>88 GT with 5spd 2850 lbs not over 3000lbs as for 0-60, 88 GT's averaged 7.7 and 1/4 mile at 15.8 Formula's which weighed in at 2740 were 7.6 and 15.6. The fastest recorded by a magazine was 7.2 and 15.4 with a stock 85 GT 4-spd. Track conditions and driver error can account for a variance of up to .4 seconds.<P>Coupes 2450 (4-cyl)<BR>Aero-Notchbacks 2560 (4-cyl)<BR>Aero-Notchbacks 2650 (V-6)<BR>Fastback GT's 2760<BR>88 coupe 2540<BR>88 Formula 2740<BR>88 GT 2850<P>The above are with manual transmissions and all available options. Auto's add 28 lbs.||||reg||1
